{"is_source_file": true, "format": "Python", "description": "This file contains processing utilities for subtitle repositioning, including OCR-based detection, handling different subtitle formats (SRT, ASS, SSA, VTT), and modifying their placement (top/bottom). It provides functions for parsing subtitle files, running OCR detection on sampled frames using OpenCV and RapidOCR, caching segment decisions, and adjusting subtitles' alignment tags accordingly. The script is designed for integration with FastAPI endpoints, supporting parallel processing with thread pools and employing caching for efficiency.", "external_files": ["cv2", "numpy", "srt"], "external_methods": ["cv2.VideoCapture", "cv2.cvtColor", "cv2.equalizeHist", "cv2.adaptiveThreshold", "cv2.CAP_PROP_FPS", "cv2.CAP_PROP_FRAME_HEIGHT", "cv2.CAP_PROP_FRAME_COUNT", "cv2.CAP_PROP_POS_FRAMES", "np.linspace", "np.clip", "np.unique", "np.asarray"], "published": ["process_subtitle"], "classes": [{"name": "VideoContext", "description": "A helper class to manage reusable video capture objects and cache video properties like fps and frame count."}], "methods": [{"name": "detect_using_rapidocr(img: np.ndarray)", "description": "Runs OCR detection on an image using RapidOCR, returns list of detected text boxes with scores.", "scope": "", "scopeKind": ""}, {"name": "str to_ass_timestamp_from_timedelta(td: timedelta)", "description": "Converts a timedelta object to ASS subtitle timestamp format.", "scope": "", "scopeKind": ""}, {"name": "np.ndarray preprocess_adaptive_threshold(image: np.ndarray)", "description": "Prepares an image for OCR by converting to grayscale, equalizing histogram, and applying adaptive thresholding.", "scope": "", "scopeKind": ""}, {"name": "float _avg_y_from_box(box: List[Tuple[float, float]])", "description": "Computes average y-coordinate from a box, which is a list of four points, as a numpy operation.", "scope": "", "scopeKind": ""}, {"name": "str decide_subtitle_position(filtered_detections_